---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { profile } from '../data/profile';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Prateek Mittal"
  description="Personal biography, background, and perspectives of Prateek Mittal."
>
  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-6 py-14 sm:py-20 space-y-12">
    
    <!-- Header with Portrait -->
    <div class="flex flex-col-reverse sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center justify-between gap-6 pb-2">
      <div class="space-y-1">
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-serif font-medium text-warm-900 dark:text-warm-50 tracking-tight">
          About Me
        </h1>
        <p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 font-sans text-sm">
          A bit more about my background, research, and interests.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="w-24 h-24 sm:w-28 sm:h-28 rounded-full overflow-hidden border-2 border-warm-200 dark:border-warm-800 shadow-sm flex-shrink-0">
        <img
          src="/images/prateek.png"
          alt="Prateek Mittal"
          class="w-full h-full object-cover"
        />
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Long-form Personal Essay -->
    <div class="space-y-6 font-serif text-lg text-stone-800 dark:text-stone-200 leading-relaxed border-t border-warm-200 dark:border-warm-800 pt-8">
      <p>
        I am an AI Decision Science Analyst and medical-AI researcher. I work across production enterprise workflows, clinical diagnostics, and high-dimensional machine learning, while exploring poetry and philosophy in my personal time.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium text-warm-900 dark:text-warm-50 pt-4">
        Medical AI & Academic Research
      </h2>
      <p>
        In research, I focus on problems where geometry and statistical theory help us interpret biological complexity. With the <strong>VEDAs Lab</strong> and my collaborators, this has led to five accepted contributions at <strong>MICCAI 2026</strong> (including three oral presentations and the MICCAI Society Travel Grant) and theoretical work on robust high-dimensional subsampling published in <strong>TMLR</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        At <strong>Yale University</strong>, I contributed to <strong>BrainLM</strong> (ICLR 2024)—a foundation model trained on 6,700 hours of fMRI recordings to decode human cognitive states from whole-brain activity.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium text-warm-900 dark:text-warm-50 pt-4">
        Industry & Decision Science
      </h2>
      <p>
        Currently, I work as an AI Decision Science Analyst within <strong>Accenture Strategy & Consulting</strong>'s AI & Data ecosystem in Gurugram, contributing to backend development, problem framing, and enterprise transformation workflows.
      </p>
      <p>
        Prior to Accenture, I was a Data Scientist – Assistant Manager at <strong>Dr. Lal PathLabs</strong>, where I built automated OCR document extraction pipelines, doctor-facing WhatsApp RAG assistants, and unified health-score frameworks tailored to Indian reference intervals.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium text-warm-900 dark:text-warm-50 pt-4">
        Ethics & Grassroots Foundations
      </h2>
      <p>
        Because technology is only as good as its safety in the hands of vulnerable patients, I founded the <strong>Foundation for Ethical AI in Healthcare</strong>—a Section 8 initiative aimed at addressing the regulatory and clinical accountability gap for clinical algorithms in India (published in <em>Health Policy and Technology</em>).
      </p>
      <p>
        Earlier during my Bachelor’s degree in Computer Engineering at Thapar Institute, I spent four formative years with <strong>Pratigya Abhiyan</strong>. Starting as a volunteer educator teaching children from daily-wage worker families and later serving as Academic Head, it grounded my understanding of education, empathy, and social responsibility.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium text-warm-900 dark:text-warm-50 pt-4">
        Poetry & The Quiet Hours
      </h2>
      <p>
        When work is done, I write poetry in Hindi and English. My writing revolves around themes of <em>भीतर का ठिकाना</em> (the inner refuge) and <em>क्षीर-नीर विवेक</em> (the classical ideal of separating essence from noise). It is how I stay grounded, thoughtful, and human.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Contact & Conversation -->
    <div class="border-t border-warm-200 dark:border-warm-800 pt-8 space-y-3 font-sans text-sm text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400">
      <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-medium text-warm-900 dark:text-warm-50">
        Get in touch
      </h3>
      <p>
        Feel free to reach out directly at <a href="mailto:prateekmittal154@gmail.com" class="text-terracotta-500 hover:underline">prateekmittal154@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>
